{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And there shall be upon every high mountain. Streams of water channels.</b> Like ועל יובל ישלח שרשיו <small>(Jeremiah 17:8)</small>, and the meaning is that the rain is abundant until it stands upon the mountains." "<b>On the day of a great slaughter, etc.</b> That people will die when towers fall, and this is consolation, for if ten die, myriads will live, for because a wall falls on a widow, HaShem does not withhold the rain from sending it to give life to many, for rain has no awareness to descend on one place and not on another alongside it."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads יובל in the Isaiah phrase as parallel to the יובל ('water channel/stream') in the Jeremiah verse he cites, both deriving from the same root."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:05.689095493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}